    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d663">

                <pb facs="0649" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg575"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Tassara to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Spain at Washington</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 11, 1865,</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, minister plenipotentiary of her Catholic Majesty, has the honor
                    to state to the honorable Secretary of State of the United States that,
                    according to a communication he has received from the captain general of Cuba,
                    there is no inconvenience on his part to the Stonewall remaining at Havana till
                    the approaching autumn, continuing at the arsenal, as the honorable Secretary
                    desired by his note of 22d July last past.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails of this occasion to reiterate to the honorable Secretary
                    of State the assurance of his highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GABRIEL G. TASSARA,</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the United States, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
